# Node / Capacitor
node_modules/
www/

# Android build outputs (the android/ project itself IS committed)
android/.gradle/
android/.idea/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/local.properties
android/app/release/

# Release signing — the keystore and its passwords. Committing either one
# hands anyone who clones the repo the ability to sign builds as PhonoLeaf,
# so these are excluded by extension anywhere in the tree, not just by path.
*.jks
*.keystore
android/keystore.properties

# IDE state (created when Android Studio opened the repo root by mistake)
.idea/

# Entitlement Worker (worker/) — local wrangler state and dev secrets.
# node_modules/ above already covers worker/node_modules/.
worker/.wrangler/
worker/.dev.vars

# Claude Design source exports — local reference copies only, never shipped
# (see CLAUDE.md's redesign section). Committing these once already caused
# a stale snapshot to nearly get treated as a recovery source for
# index.green.html; keep them local from now on.
PhonoLeaf Design System.zip
PhonoLeaf.dc.html
PhonoLeaf Redesign.dc.html
design_redesign.dc.html

# Voice pack archives. These are ~80-100 MB each and are NEVER part of the repo:
# the app downloads them at runtime and they are mirrored in R2. This rule
# exists because `wrangler r2 object get` writes the object into the CURRENT
# directory, so verifying a bucket from inside worker/ silently dropped a 98 MB
# archive into the tree, where `git add -A` swept it into a commit.
*.tar.bz2

# Installed agent skills and subagents (added 2026-09-04).
# Same treatment as node_modules: skills-lock.json is the reproducible manifest
# and is small enough to track if wanted; these directories are ~17 MB of
# THIRD-PARTY content pulled from other people's GitHub repos. This repo is
# PUBLIC, so committing them would republish someone else's work under it
# without anyone having checked their licences.
.claude/skills/
.claude/agents/
.agents/
